## Sokoban (sokoban), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   5. If a blue block is adjacent to a clear location then you can move the block onto the location.
##   6. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   7. If a location is next to an object but it is not diagonal with the object then it is adjacent to the object.
##   9. If a covered location is between a clear location and a blue block then you can move a block on the covered location onto the clear location plus move the blue block onto the covered location.
##  10. If a location is below an object then it is covered.
##  13. The goal is that a red block is on a red location and a green block is on a green location.
## World: init-sokoban.world (a grid of locations; the blue block (the pusher), a red and a green block)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator move-block (argument1 = the blue block, argument2 = the clear location), statement 5; operator push-block
##     (argument1 = the block on the covered location, argument2 = the clear location), statement 9, one proposal per
##     direction with step-1..4 static relations for "between" (A-G2); the blue block is the pusher.
##   - adjacent (statement 7) is a static relation between locations (A-G1); clear is maintained (statement 6); covered
##     (statement 10) is expanded in place (a location some block is on).
##   - The goal: a red block on a red location and a green block on a green location. "The solution has eight steps"
##     (statement 11) is checked against the plans, not used.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute object 16
production optimize-attribute on 3
production optimize-attribute below 3
production optimize-attribute clear 12
production optimize-attribute adjacent 34
production optimize-attribute step-1 8
production optimize-attribute step-2 8
production optimize-attribute step-3 9
production optimize-attribute step-4 9


## Propose initialize-sokoban when its conditions below hold.
sp {sokoban*propose*initialize-sokoban
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-sokoban ^task-operator false)
}

sp {sokoban*apply*initialize-sokoban
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-sokoban ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name sokoban ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <o-location-1> <o-location-2> <o-location-3> <o-location-4> <o-location-5> <o-location-6> <o-location-7> <o-location-8> <o-location-9> <o-location-10> <o-location-11> <o-location-12> <o-block-17> <o-block-18> <o-block-19> <o-task>)
   (<o-location-1> ^object-handle location-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 1 ^y 1 ^static true)
   (<o-location-2> ^object-handle location-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 2 ^y 1 ^color green ^static true)
   (<o-location-3> ^object-handle location-3 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 3 ^y 1 ^color red ^static true)
   (<o-location-4> ^object-handle location-4 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 1 ^y 2 ^static true)
   (<o-location-5> ^object-handle location-5 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 2 ^y 2 ^static true)
   (<o-location-6> ^object-handle location-6 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 3 ^y 2 ^static true)
